INT. DROWNED CATHEDRAL BELFRY - TIDE HOUR

Green water laps the third stair. Moonlight through broken tracery. One huge bell, furred with barnacles.

ORSOLYA (30s, salt-white braid, bone-needle at her belt) crouches on a beam. Soaked. Grinning.

KEZIAH (20s, half-fox ears, patched coat) hauls himself through the window. Drips everywhere.

ORSOLYA
You're late, Kez.

KEZIAH
The tide was early.

ORSOLYA
The tide is never early. You were.

He lifts a lantern. Inside, a trapped blue flame.

KEZIAH
Got it. Moon-ember. Off the sleeping tax-collector himself.

She snatches it. Laughs. Kisses his forehead.

ORSOLYA
Kezi. You beautiful thief.

The bell hums. Low. Wrong.

KEZIAH
Orsolya. That's not us.

She freezes. So does he.

Water rises. Fast. Knee-deep. Waist.

ORSOLYA
Take the rope.

KEZIAH
Not without you!

She shoves him. Hard. He grabs the bell-rope, swings, slams against stone. Hisses.

ORSOLYA
Ring it!

KEZIAH
It'll wake the whole drowned choir!

ORSOLYA
Better them than the tide!

He hesitates. Then pulls.

DONG. The sound rolls out like thunder under glass. The water stops. Shivers. Retreats.

Silence. They stare at each other. Then both burst out laughing.

KEZIAH
Never again.

ORSOLYA
Liar.

Somewhere below, a choir begins to sing. Off-key. Furious.

She grabs his hand. They run.
